3. The remaining 121 split as follows.

Thirty-seven are production dependencies marked `"optional": true`. Twenty-four
of those are the `@img/sharp-*` platform packages: fourteen carry LGPL and are
listed in section 4; the other ten, all 0.34.5 and all Apache-2.0, are

  @img/sharp-darwin-arm64      @img/sharp-linux-ppc64    @img/sharp-linux-x64
  @img/sharp-darwin-x64        @img/sharp-linux-riscv64  @img/sharp-linuxmusl-arm64
  @img/sharp-linux-arm         @img/sharp-linux-s390x    @img/sharp-linuxmusl-x64
  @img/sharp-linux-arm64

("Copyright 2013 Lovell Fuller and others", same upstream as section 4). These
ten are the sharp bindings only: each declares the matching LGPL-licensed
`@img/sharp-libvips-*` package as its own optional dependency, which is where
the LGPL content sits. The four win32 and wasm32 packages declare no such
dependency and carry a combined license expression instead, the libvips content
being inside them.

The remaining thirteen optional production entries are:

  @next/swc-darwin-arm64, @next/swc-darwin-x64, @next/swc-linux-arm64-gnu,
  @next/swc-linux-arm64-musl, @next/swc-linux-x64-gnu, @next/swc-linux-x64-musl,
